# Copying safely (7.8) against a fake file layer that fails at each step
# in turn. docs/design/mtp.md 7.8; 11.4 (the temporary-file and replace
# sequence). Format: ../README.md. `copy <object> to <folder> [replace]`
# runs the copy of one object into a folder of the fake file layer;
# `fail <step> [n]` makes that call fail the n-th time.
# The steps: create (CreateFile CREATE_NEW of ~MTPnnnn.TMP), write, size
# check, flush, close, move-new (temporary to target), move-old (target to
# ~MTPnnnn.OLD), move-tmp (temporary to target), delete-old, move-back
# (backup to target), delete-tmp.

case CPY-001
  title  no file of the target name: each step failing in turn
  from   7.8 steps 1 to 3
  table  fail
    a  none
    b  create
    c  create 1 (a clash: ~MTP0000.TMP exists)
    d  write 3
    e  size check
    f  flush
    g  close
    h  move-new
    i  move-new and delete-tmp
    j  device error at 50% of the data
    k  cancel at 50%
  end
  copy a.jpg (h=2, 1,000 bytes) to C:\Dest
end

case CPY-002
  title  replacing a file: each step failing in turn
  from   7.8 step 4
  table  fail
    a  none
    b  move-old (another reason than a clash)
    c  move-old 1 (a clash: ~MTP0000.OLD exists)
    d  move-tmp
    e  delete-old
    f  move-tmp and move-back
    g  move-tmp and delete-tmp
  end
  folder C:\Dest holds a.jpg (500 bytes, contents O)
  copy a.jpg (h=2, 1,000 bytes, contents N) to C:\Dest replace
end

case CPY-003
  title  sizes on the PC's disk: FAT32's ceiling of 4 GiB - 2; FAT16 by free space; any other file system nothing refused in advance
  from   7.8 (sizes on the PC's disk)
  table  fs     size
    a  FAT32  FFFFFFFEh
    b  FAT32  FFFFFFFFh
    c  FAT32  140000000h
    d  FAT    80000000h with 1 GiB free
    e  NTFS   140000000h
    f  FAT32  80000000h (the signed boundary)
  end
  copy a huge formula object of <size> to a <fs> volume
end
